1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. d4 exd4 5. O-O Nxe4 6. Re1 d5 7. Bxd5 Qxd5 8.
Nc3 Qd8 9. Nxe4 Be7 10. Bg5 Bg4 11. Bxe7 Nxe7 12. Qd3 Bxf3 13. Qxf3 O-O 14.
Rad1 b6 15. Rd3 Ng6 16. Qf5 c5 17. Rh3 h6 18. g4 Qc8 19. Nd6 Qc6 20. Re6 $2 {
"An unaccountable act of felo-de-se" wrote Staunton in the ILN.} fxe6 21. Qxe6+
Kh7 22. g5 Rae8 {Sources: Westminster Papers, 1 Apr 1873; Illustrated London
News, 5 Apr 1873; The Chess Player's Quarterly Chronicle Volume III February
1872 to December 1873 (June 1873 section); Huddersfield College Magazine, p154.
Played at the City of London CC, London.} 0-1

